{"name":"Red Cabbage","hex":"#534a77","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red cabbage","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A form of cabbage having red leaves, Brassica oleracea var. capitata f. rubra.","Food made from the leaves of the plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red_cabbage"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red cabbage","blocks":[{"text":"The red cabbage is a kind of cabbage, also known as Blaukraut after preparation. Its leaves are coloured dark red/purple. However, the plant changes its colour according to the pH value of the soil due to a pigment belonging to anthocyanins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Brassica_oleracea_var_capitata_Rubyball.jpg/330px-Brassica_oleracea_var_capitata_Rubyball.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_cabbage"},{"title":"Cabbage","blocks":[{"text":"Cabbage, comprising several cultivars of Brassica oleracea, is a leafy green, red (purple), or white biennial plant grown as an annual vegetable crop for its dense-leaved heads. It is descended from the wild cabbage, and belongs to the \"cole crops\" or brassicas, meaning it is closely related to broccoli and cauliflower ; Brussels sprouts ; and Savoy cabbage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Cabbage_and_cross_section_on_white.jpg/330px-Cabbage_and_cross_section_on_white.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabbage"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Tussen_Finningen_en_M%C3%B6rslingen%2C_veld_met_rode_kolen_foto9_2016-08-03_15.25.jpg/500px-Tussen_Finningen_en_M%C3%B6rslingen%2C_veld_met_rode_kolen_foto9_2016-08-03_15.25.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Tussen_Finningen_en_M%C3%B6rslingen%2C_veld_met_rode_kolen_foto9_2016-08-03_15.25.jpg/1280px-Tussen_Finningen_en_M%C3%B6rslingen%2C_veld_met_rode_kolen_foto9_2016-08-03_15.25.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Tussen_Finningen_en_M%C3%B6rslingen%2C_veld_met_rode_kolen_foto9_2016-08-03_15.25.jpg/500px-Tussen_Finningen_en_M%C3%B6rslingen%2C_veld_met_rode_kolen_foto9_2016-08-03_15.25.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red cabbage in panorama between Finningen and Mörslingen, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATussen_Finningen_en_M%C3%B6rslingen%2C_veld_met_rode_kolen_foto9_2016-08-03_15.25.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Purple_cabbage.jpg/330px-Purple_cabbage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Purple_cabbage.jpg/330px-Purple_cabbage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red cabbage","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APurple_cabbage.jpg"},{"srcset":